> Anyway, what sort of armour is good for a wizard (doesn't hinder
> spellcasting)?

Mithril does hinder spell casting, but if I get mithril early I will
where
it for a while until something better comes along and settle for using
thrown daggers as my primary weapon.  Early wizards need to get
to expert at throwing daggers early in the game anyways so early
enough and the spell interference doesn't matter.

The next type of armor to be interested in is studded leather.  It
does not interfere with spell casting but you'll want additional
pieces
to make up for its lower armor class.  Leather gloves, elven leather
helmet, elven boots or jackboots are good when combined with a
studded leather armor.  That combination can be gotten early on
and then replace them one by one over time.

One type of armor that does not interfere with spell casting and that
does give good AC is crystal plate mail.  It's too heavy for almost
anyone to wear for any length of time.

My favorite wizard armor set is -

blessed fireproof +5 teeshirt, blessed +5 gray dragon scale mail,
blessed amulet of reflection, blessed fireproof +5 robe,
blessed fireproof +5 gauntlets of dexerity, blessed fireproof +5
boots of speed or jumping, blessed rustproof +5 helm of brillinace
or blessed fireproof +5 cornathum.

Common alternative is shirt, silver dragon scale mail, "oLS,
cloak of MR, gloves, boots, hat.

